les.\n\n# Step 3: Apply the z-score normalization on the SCALED_VARIANCE_ALONG_MINOR_AXIS feature.\ndf['SCALED_VARIANCE_ALONG_MINOR_AXIS_ZSCORE'] = (df['SCALED_VARIANCE_ALONG_MINOR_AXIS'] - df['SCALED_VARIANCE_ALONG_MINOR_AXIS'].mean()) / df['SCALED_VARIANCE_ALONG_MINOR_AXIS'].std()\n# Usefulness: Normalizing this feature can help improve its interpretation and scale consistency when combined with other features, especially since it has relatively high variance and a wide range.\n```end\n\n```python\n# Explanation why the column SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS is dropped\ndf.drop(columns=['SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS'], inplace=True)\n# This column has a very narrow range (0-22) and low variance (Std = 5.0030). It might add little value to classification, carrying redundant or insignificant information.\n\n# Explanation why the column HOLLOWS_RATIO is dropped\ndf.drop(columns=['HOLLOWS_RATIO'], inplace=True)\n# HOLLOWS_RATIO has a tight and relatively high range (181-211) with low variability (Std = 7.2775). Its low spread suggests it provides limited discriminatory power for classification.\n\n# Explanation why the column PR.AXIS_RECTANGULARITY is dropped\ndf.drop(columns=['PR.AXIS_RECTANGULARITY'], inplace=True)\n# This feature has a significantly tight range (17-29) and low standard deviation (Std = 2.5590), indicating it may not add meaningful variance for classifying the vehicles.\n```end\n\n```python\n# Step 4: Generate a feature that represents an interaction between PR.AXIS_ASPECT_RATIO and MAX.LENGTH_ASPECT_RATIO\ndf['ASPECT_RATIO_INTERACTION'] = df['PR.AXIS_ASPECT_RATIO'] * df['MAX.LENGTH_ASPECT_RATIO']\n# Usefulness: By multiplying these two aspect-ratio-based features, this interaction might help capture differences between elongated and compact vehicle silhouettes, aiding in distinguishing vehicle types.\n\n# Step 5: Calculate the cube of SCATTER_RATIO to enhance variance in this feature.\ndf['SCATTER_RATIO_CUBE'] = df['SCATTER_RATIO'] ** 3\n# Usefulness: Elevating SCATTER_RATIO to the power of 3 can help highlight disparities in its values, especially because it’s a key indicator of the spread of the silhouette, which can tie closely to specific vehicle shapes.\n\n# Step 6: Add a binary feature indicating whether COMPACTNESS is greater than a threshold (e.g., median of the COMPACTNESS feature).\ndf['COMPACTNESS_HIGH'] = (df['COMPACTNESS'] > df['COMPACTNESS'].median()).astype(int)\n# Usefulness: This binary indicator can help the model identify vehicles with disproportionately high or low COMPACTNESS, linking to unique silhouette characteristics.\n```end"]
